00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:56.830
So, this feature covers the newborn baby.

00:27:56.854 --> 00:28:00.893
As for adding the baby to the policy,
that can be done only after 91 days.

00:28:01.401 --> 00:28:02.528
We’ve now gone through these features.

00:28:02.552 --> 00:28:04.941
Next comes the eligibility for this policy.

00:28:04.965 --> 00:28:10.823
Only females aged 18 to
75 years can buy this policy.

00:28:10.847 --> 00:28:13.196
A 10-year-old female cannot
buy this particular policy.

00:28:13.220 --> 00:28:18.402
This applies only to this
policy—other policies are different.

00:28:18.593 --> 00:28:22.013
In general, even a one-year-old child can
be covered under a health insurance policy.

00:28:22.037 --> 00:28:25.108
It’s not mandatory that the minimum
age must be 18 for health insurance.

00:28:25.337 --> 00:28:28.559
This age restriction is
specific to this policy.

00:28:28.583 --> 00:28:33.346
Otherwise, about 99% of policies
can be purchased for people of any age,

00:28:33.370 --> 00:28:36.520
even for a one-year-old.

00:28:37.400 --> 00:28:41.355
Next is the floater sum insured:
adults aged 18 to 75 years.

00:28:41.379 --> 00:28:43.109
That means if you take
a family floater policy,

00:28:43.133 --> 00:28:45.339
the adults included must be
between 18 and 75 years of age.

00:28:45.363 --> 00:28:51.952
Children can be added, but at least
one female member must be included.

00:28:52.254 --> 00:28:56.937
If you add children, they
must be at least 91 days old.

00:28:56.961 --> 00:29:00.587
For a family floater, the child’s
age must be a minimum of 91 days.

00:29:01.078 --> 00:29:04.912
A child can stay covered under
the policy until the age of 25.

00:29:05.348 --> 00:29:12.279
If it’s a boy child, he can
remain covered until he turns 25,

00:29:12.596 --> 00:29:20.926
after which he must exit the policy and
will be issued a separate individual policy.

00:29:21.450 --> 00:29:23.934
However, one important thing: it’s
better not to add a son to this policy,

00:29:23.958 --> 00:29:26.806
because later he won’t be able to get
this same policy as an individual policy,

00:29:26.831 --> 00:29:28.831
since this is a women-only policy.

00:29:29.005 --> 00:29:32.243
If you have a daughter, there’s no issue.

00:29:32.267 --> 00:29:35.076
A daughter can stay covered
even after 25, up to 30 years of age,

00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:37.203
if she is unemployed and
not financially independent.

00:29:37.227 --> 00:29:42.592
For example, if parents take a floater
policy and add their daughter after 91 days,

00:29:43.250 --> 00:29:45.045
she can remain covered until the age of 30.

00:29:45.236 --> 00:29:49.188
After 30, she will need to take the
same policy as an individual policy.

00:29:50.585 --> 00:29:54.816
But again, avoid adding a son
in such women-specific policies,

00:29:54.840 --> 00:30:01.079
because it can create issues for him later,
as the policy is meant only for females.

00:30:03.745 --> 00:30:05.922
Next, one of the features
is air ambulance charges.

00:30:05.946 --> 00:30:12.833
If someone needs an air ambulance, coverage
is provided up to 10% of the sum insured.

00:30:12.858 --> 00:30:14.276
That means if the policy cover is ₹25 lakh,

00:30:14.300 --> 00:30:16.300
air ambulance expenses
will be covered up to ₹2.5 lakh.

00:30:16.784 --> 00:30:21.810
This benefit is available only for sum
insured options of ₹10 lakh and above.

00:30:21.834 --> 00:30:24.809
In other words, you cannot say that if you
have a ₹5 lakh policy, you should get 10%—

00:30:24.833 --> 00:30:27.602
₹50,000—as air ambulance cover.

00:30:27.626 --> 00:30:29.958
The policy must be at
least ₹10 lakh or more.

00:30:29.982 --> 00:30:32.846
Moving ahead, let’s talk
about network hospitals.

00:30:32.870 --> 00:30:34.512
Let me explain this with an example.

00:30:34.836 --> 00:30:37.900
I’ve added some screenshots showing
different health insurance companies

00:30:38.003 --> 00:30:42.297
and their network hospitals.

00:30:42.708 --> 00:30:44.836
For instance, Care Health Insurance has the

00:30:44.860 --> 00:30:47.995
highest number of network hospitals
across the country—more than 16,500.

00:30:48.678 --> 00:30:50.678
But if someone lives in Delhi NCR,

00:30:50.955 --> 00:30:53.939
Care Health does not have
the highest number there.

00:30:53.963 --> 00:30:55.454
In Delhi NCR, Care has
around 650 hospitals,

00:30:55.478 --> 00:30:58.533
while some other insurers
have more—around 900 or 850.

00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:02.215
So you shouldn’t blindly look at
nationwide numbers and conclude that

00:31:02.239 --> 00:31:06.937
Care is the best just because it has
the most network hospitals across India.

00:31:07.174 --> 00:31:10.691
You need to check which insurer has the
most network hospitals in your own area.

00:31:11.499 --> 00:31:13.009
For example, if I live in Chandigarh,

00:31:13.033 --> 00:31:17.906
I’ll check which insurance company has
the most network hospitals in Chandigarh.

00:31:17.930 --> 00:31:20.517
What’s the point of looking at numbers
for Tamil Nadu if I don’t live there?

00:31:20.826 --> 00:31:21.763
These are practical things to keep in mind.

00:31:21.787 --> 00:31:24.192
I’m giving you a final overview here.

00:31:24.407 --> 00:31:26.803
I’ve also added screenshots showing

00:31:27.096 --> 00:31:30.239
pre-hospitalization and post-hospitalization
coverage for different companies.

00:31:30.263 --> 00:31:35.493
Some offer 30 days, some 60 days,
and some even 180 days.

00:31:35.517 --> 00:31:37.739
You can compare these features easily.

00:31:38.730 --> 00:31:42.135
Then there is the claim settlement
ratio and the incurred claim ratio—

00:31:42.160 --> 00:31:43.231
these are a bit technical, but important.

00:31:43.255 --> 00:31:44.040
Generally,

00:31:44.357 --> 00:31:48.182
we say that a company with a higher
claim settlement ratio is a good company.

00:31:48.206 --> 00:32:03.694
For example, if an insurance company
receives 100 claims and approves 99 of them,

00:32:03.932 --> 00:32:06.313
its claim settlement ratio is 99%.

00:32:06.503 --> 00:32:08.217
But if another company receives 100 claims

00:32:08.241 --> 00:32:12.590
and approves only 80 while rejecting
20, its claim settlement ratio is 80%.

00:32:12.614 --> 00:32:16.606
Such a company is considered poor because
it rejects too many claims unnecessarily.

00:32:16.804 --> 00:32:19.487
So, companies with higher claim
settlement ratios are usually better.

00:32:19.511 --> 00:32:24.379
For instance, if one has 99%,
another has 98.5%, or 98.17%,

00:32:24.403 --> 00:32:25.919
you can check and compare them like this.

00:32:26.181 --> 00:32:27.641
The incurred claim ratio works like this:

00:32:27.665 --> 00:32:30.467
suppose the company does
not receive 100 individual claims,

00:32:30.491 --> 00:32:32.362
but claims worth a total amount,
let’s say the total claim amount is ₹100.

00:32:32.966 --> 00:32:36.426
Actually, ₹100 is not a very good example,
but just assume it for understanding.

00:32:36.450 --> 00:32:39.917
Let’s say, in a year, the company
receives total claims worth ₹100 crore.

00:32:40.647 --> 00:32:48.418
Out of this ₹100 crore, the company
approves and pays claims worth ₹70 crore.

00:32:48.616 --> 00:32:49.775
That company is doing fine.

00:32:50.148 --> 00:32:55.816
Ideally, the incurred claim ratio
should be in the range of 60% to 75%.

00:32:56.006 --> 00:32:56.434
Why?

00:32:56.679 --> 00:33:03.775
Because if claims worth ₹100 crore come
in and the company pays out ₹99 crore,

00:33:04.060 --> 00:33:05.703
how much money is left with the company?

00:33:05.728 --> 00:33:06.361
Only ₹1 crore.

00:33:06.463 --> 00:33:09.162
From that, the company still has to
spend on advertising, office operations,

00:33:09.186 --> 00:33:10.988
employee salaries, and other expenses.

00:33:11.218 --> 00:33:15.012
Suppose those expenses come to ₹10 crore.

00:33:15.273 --> 00:33:16.859
₹99 crore worth of claims were paid.

00:33:16.884 --> 00:33:20.800
Then the total outgo becomes ₹109
crore, while income is only ₹100 crore.

00:33:20.950 --> 00:33:22.950
Such a company will shut down very quickly.

00:33:23.600 --> 00:33:28.212
That’s why a company with an incurred
claim ratio between 60% and 75%

00:33:28.236 --> 00:33:29.863
is considered the best.

00:33:30.792 --> 00:33:34.689
Now, coming back to
where we started the video—

00:33:34.713 --> 00:33:38.609
I hope you’ll never actually
need to use this information.

00:33:39.307 --> 00:33:43.347
The reason is that I had
listed some features earlier,

00:33:43.505 --> 00:33:46.926
like the pre-existing disease cover
for HDFC ERGO and Care Supreme.

00:33:47.807 --> 00:33:52.925
HDFC ERGO has a pre-existing
disease waiting period of 3 years.

00:33:53.171 --> 00:33:54.364
Care Supreme also has
a 3-year waiting period.

00:33:54.388 --> 00:33:56.388
But Care Supreme is more popular,

00:33:56.713 --> 00:33:58.555
and for people who already
have a pre-existing disease,

00:33:58.579 --> 00:34:01.142
Care Supreme generally works better.

00:34:01.277 --> 00:34:02.475
Niva Bupa has a 4-year waiting period,

00:34:02.499 --> 00:34:04.872
which can be a drawback for
someone who already has a disease.

00:34:05.078 --> 00:34:07.403
Aditya Birla has a waiting
period of 3 to 4 years—

00:34:07.427 --> 00:34:13.302
this range depends on the type of disease.

00:34:13.938 --> 00:34:15.938
For mild conditions, it may be 3 years,

00:34:15.962 --> 00:34:18.207
and for more serious
conditions, it can go up to 4 years.

00:34:18.334 --> 00:34:20.127
Some others also have a 4-year waiting
period, and some have 3 to 4 years.

00:34:20.152 --> 00:34:21.872
So, for someone who already
has a medical condition,

00:34:21.896 --> 00:34:22.974
these two options become the best choices.

00:34:23.061 --> 00:34:24.418
Similarly, you can
compare restoration benefits.

00:34:24.442 --> 00:34:27.441
One policy offers a 100% restoration
benefit, another also offers 100%,

00:34:27.465 --> 00:34:29.163
another offers unlimited restoration,

00:34:29.187 --> 00:34:32.028
another offers limited restoration,
and some again offer 100%.

00:34:32.877 --> 00:34:35.845
In the same way, you can compare
pre- and post-hospitalization expenses

00:34:35.869 --> 00:34:39.853
and all other features across policies.

00:34:40.495 --> 00:34:42.495
By now,

00:34:42.519 --> 00:34:46.670
you should clearly understand how to
read and analyze health insurance policies.

00:34:46.742 --> 00:34:48.845
Once any health policy
comes in front of you,

00:34:48.869 --> 00:34:50.869
